% Providers: openalex, wos, scopus, ieee live; s2 key rejected (HTTP 403);
% dblp returned a bot-challenge page (non-JSON) to every query, so its cells
% are provider-down, not zero. Each query run with -l 50 per provider.
% FC := ("flipped classroom" OR "inverted classroom" OR "flipped learning")
% S1: FC AND (meta-analysis OR "systematic review") AND (achievement OR
%     "learning outcomes" OR performance)
% S2: FC AND (programming OR "computer science" OR computing) AND
%     (achievement OR "learning outcomes" OR performance OR grades)
% S3: FC AND (programming OR "computer science" OR computing) AND
%     (meta-analysis OR "systematic review" OR "literature review")
% C1: FC AND (meta-analysis OR "systematic review") AND ("publication bias"
%     OR heterogeneity OR "no significant difference" OR moderator OR
%     moderators OR limitations)
% C2: FC AND (programming OR "computer science" OR computing) AND
%     ("no significant difference" OR "no difference" OR challenges OR
%     resistance OR negative)
% C3: S3 AND ("no significant difference" OR heterogeneity OR limitations
%     OR "mixed results")
% P1: (FC OR "active learning") AND (lecture OR lectures) AND ("student
%     perception" OR "student perceptions" OR satisfaction OR preference OR
%     preferences OR resistance OR "feeling of learning")
% P2: (FC OR "active learning") AND ("perceived learning" OR "feeling of
%     learning" OR "self-reported learning") AND (lecture OR lectures OR
%     passive)
% P1w: P1 with truncation where the provider supports it: (FC OR "active
%     learning") AND lecture* AND ("student perception*" OR satisfaction OR
%     preference* OR resistance OR "feeling of learning"); run on ieee, wos,
%     scopus (OpenAlex cannot truncate inside phrases; P1 is its form).
% WoS ran TS=(<query>), Scopus TITLE-ABS-KEY(<query>), OpenAlex and IEEE
% the query as is; DBLP got keyword reductions (all failed).
% Full texts are in scholar's PDF cache (~/.cache/scholar/pdfs/<hash>.pdf)
% or, where only HTML/XML existed, Europe PMC full-text XML (URL given).

% === provenance: LagSaele2019 ===
% CLAIM: Flipped classroom vs lecture-based teaching gives a small positive
%   effect on learning in a meta-analysis across levels and disciplines;
%   smaller after correcting for small-study bias; satisfaction ~ zero.
% FOUND-VIA: scholar search C1 -n flipped-classroom-learning -p openalex
%   -l 50 (2026-10-07). Full text: ERIC copy
%   https://files.eric.ed.gov/fulltext/EJ1229661.pdf via fetch_pdf.py
%   (cache 806e149e8de062be.pdf); publisher PDF 403.
% PICKED: largest broad meta-analysis with explicit small-study-bias
%   correction (k = 272, all disciplines), only one reporting pass rates.
% QUOTE (p. 1, abstract): "Our results indicate a small effect in favor of
%   the flipped classroom on learning (Hedges' g = 0.35, 95% confidence
%   interval [CI] [0.31, 0.40], k = 272). However, analyses restricted to
%   studies with sufficient power resulted in an estimate of 0.24 (95% CI
%   [0.18, 0.31], k = 90). Effects on pass rates (odds ratio = 1.55 ...) and
%   student satisfaction (Hedges' g = 0.16 ...) were small and also likely
%   influenced by publication bias."
% QUOTE (p. 7): "I2 = 82.97" (learning); STEM g = 0.32 vs humanities 0.54;
%   test of preparation g = 0.40 vs 0.31, "only marginally statistically
%   significant (Q = 3.8, p = .051)".
% QUOTE (p. 9): "A trim-and-fill adjustment yields an estimate of 0.17
%   [0.12, 0.22]. Together, these adjustments suggest that the true weighted
%   mean effect is somewhere around one fifth of a standard deviation."
%   Satisfaction "changes from 0.16 to -0.03 (95% CI [-0.14, 0.08])".
% QUOTE (p. 12): "Thus, students may dislike an educational intervention
%   even though it improves learning."
% VERIFIED: full text read (abstract, results pp. 7-9, discussion
%   pp. 11-13). Pages are the journal's printed folios.
% COUNTER: C1 on all live providers; qualifying work below (Kapur2022,
%   Hew2021methodology); the paper itself reports bias and heterogeneity.
% DATE: 2026-10-07
@article{LagSaele2019,
  author  = {L{\aa}g, Torstein and S{\ae}le, Rannveig Gr{\o}m},
  title   = {Does the Flipped Classroom Improve Student Learning and
